ullcrdt_ind>false</bbmd_canvas_fullcrdt_ind><bbmd_all_fullcredit_ind>false</bbmd_all_fullcredit_ind><bbmd_numbertype>none</bbmd_numbertype><bbmd_partialcredit/><bbmd_orientationtype>vertical</bbmd_orientationtype><bbmd_is_extracredit>false</bbmd_is_extracredit><bbmd_ai_state>No</bbmd_ai_state><qmd_absolutescore_max>1.000000000000000</qmd_absolutescore_max><qmd_weighting>0</qmd_weighting><qmd_instructornotes/></itemmetadata><presentation><flow class="Block"><flow class="QUESTION_BLOCK"><flow class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="HTML">________ is a short presentation, usually delivered in 30 seconds to one minute (about the time you spend in a large office elevator).</mat_formattedtext></mat_extension></material></flow></flow><flow class="RESPONSE_BLOCK"><response_str ident="response" rcardinality="Single" rtiming="No"><render_fib charset="us-ascii" encoding="UTF_8" rows="8" columns="127" maxchars="0" prompt="Box" fibtype="String" minnumber="0" maxnumber="0"/></response_str></flow></flow></presentation><resprocessing scoremodel="SumOfScores"><outcomes><decvar varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal" defaultval="0.0" minvalue="0.0" maxvalue="1.00"/></outcomes><respcondition title="correct"><conditionvar/><setvar variablename="SCORE" action="Set">SCORE.max</setvar><displayfeedback linkrefid="correct" feedbacktype="Response"/></respcondition><respcondition title="incorrect"><conditionvar><other/></conditionvar><setvar variablename="SCORE" action="Set">0.0</setvar><displayfeedback linkrefid="incorrect" feedbacktype="Response"/></respcondition></resprocessing><itemfeedback ident="correct" view="All"><flow_mat class="Block"><flow_mat class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="SMART_TEXT"/></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="incorrect" view="All"><flow_mat class="Block"><flow_mat class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="SMART_TEXT"/></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="solution" view="All"><solution view="All" feedbackstyle="Complete"><solutionmaterial><flow_mat class="Block"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="HTML">An elevator pitch</mat_formattedtext></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></solutionmaterial></solution></itemfeedback></item><item maxattempts="0"><itemmetadata><bbmd_asi_object_id>_188168_1</bbmd_asi_object_id><bbmd_asitype>Item</bbmd_asitype><bbmd_assessmenttype>Test</bbmd_assessmenttype><bbmd_sectiontype>Subsection</bbmd_sectiontype><bbmd_questiontype>Essay</bbmd_questiontype><bbmd_is_from_cartridge>false</bbmd_is_from_cartridge><bbmd_is_disabled>false</bbmd_is_disabled><bbmd_negative_points_ind>N</bbmd_negative_points_ind><bbmd_canvas_fullcrdt_ind>false</bbmd_canvas_fullcrdt_ind><bbmd_all_fullcredit_ind>false</bbmd_all_fullcredit_ind><bbmd_numbertype>none</bbmd_numbertype><bbmd_partialcredit/><bbmd_orientationtype>vertical</bbmd_orientationtype><bbmd_is_extracredit>false</bbmd_is_extracredit><bbmd_ai_state>No</bbmd_ai_state><qmd_absolutescore_max>1.000000000000000</qmd_absolutescore_max><qmd_weighting>0</qmd_weighting><qmd_instructornotes/></itemmetadata><presentation><flow class="Block"><flow class="QUESTION_BLOCK"><flow class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="HTML">If a presenter has thoroughly prepared for his or her presentation, he or she should be able to effectively handle any kind of question. Is this statement correct? Why or why not? How would dealing with the Q&amp;amp;A of the interested but neutral audience differ from a worried audience?</mat_formattedtext></mat_extension></material></flow></flow><flow class="RESPONSE_BLOCK"><response_str ident="response" rcardinality="Single" rtiming="No"><render_fib charset="us-ascii" encoding="UTF_8" rows="8" columns="127" maxchars="0" prompt="Box" fibtype="String" minnumber="0" maxnumber="0"/></response_str></flow></flow></presentation><resprocessing scoremodel="SumOfScores"><outcomes><decvar varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal" defaultval="0.0" minvalue="0.0" maxvalue="1.00"/></outcomes><respcondition title="correct"><conditionvar/><setvar variablename="SCORE" action="Set">SCORE.max</setvar><displayfeedback linkrefid="correct" feedbacktype="Response"/></respcondition><respcondition title="incorrect"><conditionvar><other/></conditionvar><setvar variablename="SCORE" action="Set">0.0</setvar><displayfeedback linkrefid="incorrect" feedbacktype="Response"/></respcondition></resprocessing><itemfeedback ident="correct" view="All"><flow_mat class="Block"><flow_mat class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="SMART_TEXT"/></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="incorrect" view="All"><flow_mat class="Block"><flow_mat class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="SMART_TEXT"/></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="solution" view="All"><solution view="All" feedbackstyle="Complete"><solutionmaterial><flow_mat class="Block"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="HTML">Being thoroughly prepared definitely gives the presenter the confidence to handle questions, but he or she may not be able to answer all of them effectively. It helps to be aware of the audience&amp;#x27;s concerns, keep one&amp;#x27;s cool while answering difficult questions, and respond diplomatically and honestly. If the presenter does not have an answer to an important question, he or she should offer to provide it after the presentation.&lt;br&gt;In the case of the interested but neutral audience, address whatever objections that they may have, use the Q&amp;amp;A round to direct their interest into a lively discussion, and encourage dialogue rather than making it a one-man show.&lt;br&gt;In the case of a worried audience, acknowledge their fears and their feelings and use the direct approach (for good news) and indirect approach (for bad news) appropriately, while answering their queries with honesty.</mat_formattedtext></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></solutionmaterial></solution></itemfeedback></item><item maxattempts="0"><itemmetadata><bbmd_asi_object_id>_188169_1</bbmd_asi_object_id><bbmd_asitype>Item</bbmd_asitype><bbmd_assessmenttype>Test</bbmd_assessmenttype><bbmd_sectiontype>Subsection</bbmd_sectiontype><bbmd_questiontype>Essay</bbmd_questiontype><bbmd_is_from_cartridge>false</bbmd_is_from_cartridge><bbmd_is_disabled>false</bbmd_is_disabled><bbmd_negative_points_ind>N</bbmd_negative_points_ind><bbmd_canvas_fullcrdt_ind>false</bbmd_canvas_fullcrdt_ind><bbmd_all_fullcredit_ind>false</bbmd_all_fullcredit_ind><bbmd_numbertype>none</bbmd_numbertype><bbmd_partialcredit/><bbmd_orientationtype>vertical</bbmd_orientationtype><bbmd_is_extracredit>false</bbmd_is_extracredit><bbmd_ai_state>No</bbmd_ai_state><qmd_absolutescore_max>1.000000000000000</qmd_absolutescore_max><qmd_weighting>0</qmd_weighting><qmd_instructornotes/></itemmetadata><presentation><flow class="Block"><flow class="QUESTION_BLOCK"><flow class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="HTML">Describe ten suggestions for becoming a more confident speaker.</mat_formattedtext></mat_extension></material></flow></flow><flow class="RESPONSE_BLOCK"><response_str ident="response" rcardinality="Single" rtiming="No"><render_fib charset="us-ascii" encoding="UTF_8" rows="8" columns="127" maxchars="0" prompt="Box" fibtype="String" minnumber="0" maxnumber="0"/></response_str></flow></flow></presentation><resprocessing scoremodel="SumOfScores"><outcomes><decvar varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal" defaultval="0.0" minvalue="0.0" maxvalue="1.00"/></outcomes><respcondition title="correct"><conditionvar/><setvar variablename="SCORE" action="Set">SCORE.max</setvar><displayfeedback linkrefid="correct" feedbacktype="Response"/></respcondition><respcondition title="incorrect"><conditionvar><other/></conditionvar><setvar variablename="SCORE" action="Set">0.0</setvar><displayfeedback linkrefid="incorrect" feedbacktype="Response"/></respcondition></resprocessing><itemfeedback ident="correct" view="All"><flow_mat class="Block"><flow_mat class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="SMART_TEXT"/></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="incorrect" view="All"><flow_mat class="Block"><flow_mat class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="SMART_TEXT"/></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="solution" view="All"><solution view="All" feedbackstyle="Complete"><solutionmaterial><flow_mat class="Block"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="HTML">1. Think positively. Imagine yourself giving a polished and professional presentation. 2. Prepare more material than necessary. Extra knowledge will reduce your anxiety. 3. Rehearse. The more familiar you are with your material, the less nervous you will be. 4. Visualize your success. Use the few minutes before you start to tell yourself that you&amp;#x27;re ready. 5. Breath. 6. Be ready. Have your first sentence memorized and ready to go. 7. Be comfortable. 8. Take a three-second break. If you find yourself racing, pause, breathe, and perhaps reshuffle your notes. 9. Focus on your message and audience. Think about your subject and your audience. 10. Maintain eye contact with friendly audience members.</mat_formattedtext></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></solutionmaterial></solution></itemfeedback></item><item maxattempts="0"><itemmetadata><bbmd_asi_object_id>_188170_1</bbmd_asi_object_id><bbmd_asitype>Item</bbmd_asitype><bbmd_assessmenttype>Test</bbmd_assessmenttype><bbmd_sectiontype>Subsection</bbmd_sectiontype><bbmd_questiontype>Essay</bbmd_questiontype><bbmd_is_from_cartridge>false</bbmd_is_from_cartridge><bbmd_is_disabled>false</bbmd_is_disabled><bbmd_negative_points_ind>N</bbmd_negative_points_ind><bbmd_canvas_fullcrdt_ind>false</bbmd_canvas_fullcrdt_ind><bbmd_all_fullcredit_ind>false</bbmd_all_fullcredit_ind><bbmd_numbertype>none</bbmd_numbertype><bbmd_partialcredit/><bbmd_orientationtype>vertical</bbmd_orientationtype><bbmd_is_extracredit>false</bbmd_is_extracredit><bbmd_ai_state>No</bbmd_ai_state><qmd_absolutescore_max>1.000000000000000</qmd_absolutescore_max><qmd_weighting>0</qmd_weighting><qmd_instructornotes/></itemmetadata><presentation><flow class="Block"><flow class="QUESTION_BLOCK"><flow class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="HTML">List and explain five tips for embracing the backchannel during a presentation.</mat_formattedtext></mat_extension></material></flow></flow><flow class="RESPONSE_BLOCK"><response_str ident="response" rcardinality="Single" rtiming="No"><render_fib charset="us-ascii" encoding="UTF_8" rows="8" columns="127" maxchars="0" prompt="Box" fibtype="String" minnumber="0" maxnumber="0"/></response_str></flow></flow></presentation><resprocessing scoremodel="SumOfScores"><outcomes><decvar varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal" defaultval="0.0" minvalue="0.0" maxvalue="1.00"/></outcomes><respcondition title="correct"><conditionvar/><setvar variablename="SCORE" action="Set">SCORE.max</setvar><displayfeedback linkrefid="correct" feedbacktype="Response"/></respcondition><respcondition title="incorrect"><conditionvar><other/></conditionvar><setvar variablename="SCORE" action="Set">0.0</setvar><displayfeedback linkrefid="incorrect" feedbacktype="Response"/></respcondition></resprocessing><itemfeedback ident="correct" view="All"><flow_mat class="Block"><flow_mat class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="SMART_TEXT"/></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="incorrect" view="All"><flow_mat class="Block"><flow_mat class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="SMART_TEXT"/></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></flow_mat></itemfeedback></item><item maxattempts="0"><itemmetadata><bbmd_asi_object_id>_188171_1</bbmd_asi_object_id><bbmd_asitype>Item</bbmd_asitype><bbmd_assessmenttype>Test</bbmd_assessmenttype><bbmd_sectiontype>Subsection</bbmd_sectiontype><bbmd_questiontype>Essay</bbmd_questiontype><bbmd_is_from_cartridge>false</bbmd_is_from_cartridge><bbmd_is_disabled>false</bbmd_is_disabled><bbmd_negative_points_ind>N</bbmd_negative_points_ind><bbmd_canvas_fullcrdt_ind>false</bbmd_canvas_fullcrdt_ind><bbmd_all_fullcredit_ind>false</bbmd_all_fullcredit_ind><bbmd_numbertype>none</bbmd_numbertype><bbmd_partialcredit/><bbmd_orientationtype>vertical</bbmd_orientationtype><bbmd_is_extracredit>false</bbmd_is_extracredit><bbmd_ai_state>No</bbmd_ai_state><qmd_absolutescore_max>1.000000000000000</qmd_absolutescore_max><qmd_weighting>0</qmd_weighting><qmd_instructornotes/></itemmetadata><presentation><flow class="Block"><flow class="QUESTION_BLOCK"><flow class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="HTML">List and explain five tips for giving presentations online.</mat_formattedtext></mat_extension></material></flow></flow><flow class="RESPONSE_BLOCK"><response_str ident="response" rcardinality="Single" rtiming="No"><render_fib charset="us-ascii" encoding="UTF_8" rows="8" columns="127" maxchars="0" prompt="Box" fibtype="String" minnumber="0" maxnumber="0"/></response_str></flow></flow></presentation><resprocessing scoremodel="SumOfScores"><outcomes><decvar varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal" defaultval="0.0" minvalue="0.0" maxvalue="1.00"/></outcomes><respcondition title="correct"><conditionvar/><setvar variablename="SCORE" action="Set">SCORE.max</setvar><displayfeedback linkrefid="correct" feedbacktype="Response"/></respcondition><respcondition title="incorrect"><conditionvar><other/></conditionvar><setvar variablename="SCORE" action="Set">0.0</setvar><displayfeedback linkrefid="incorrect" feedbacktype="Response"/></respcondition></resprocessing><itemfeedback ident="correct" view="All"><flow_mat class="Block"><flow_mat class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="SMART_TEXT"/></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="incorrect" view="All"><flow_mat class="Block"><flow_mat class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="SMART_TEXT"/></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></flow_mat></itemfeedback></item><item maxattempts="0"><itemmetadata><bbmd_asi_object_id>_188172_1</bbmd_asi_object_id><bbmd_asitype>Item</bbmd_asitype><bbmd_assessmenttype>Test</bbmd_assessmenttype><bbmd_sectiontype>Subsection</bbmd_sectiontype><bbmd_questiontype>Essay</bbmd_questiontype><bbmd_is_from_cartridge>false</bbmd_is_from_cartridge><bbmd_is_disabled>false</bbmd_is_disabled><bbmd_negative_points_ind>N</bbmd_negative_points_ind><bbmd_canvas_fullcrdt_ind>false</bbmd_canvas_fullcrdt_ind><bbmd_all_fullcredit_ind>false</bbmd_all_fullcredit_ind><bbmd_numbertype>none</bbmd_numbertype><bbmd_partialcredit/><bbmd_orientationtype>vertical</bbmd_orientationtype><bbmd_is_extracredit>false</bbmd_is_extracredit><bbmd_ai_state>No</bbmd_ai_state><qmd_absolutescore_max>1.000000000000000</qmd_absolutescore_max><qmd_weighting>0</qmd_weighting><qmd_instructornotes/></itemmetadata><presentation><flow class="Block"><flow class="QUESTION_BLOCK"><flow class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="HTML">What is an elevator pitch and when could or should you use one?</mat_formattedtext></mat_extension></material></flow></flow><flow class="RESPONSE_BLOCK"><response_str ident="response" rcardinality="Single" rtiming="No"><render_fib charset="us-ascii" encoding="UTF_8" rows="8" columns="127" maxchars="0" prompt="Box" fibtype="String" minnumber="0" maxnumber="0"/></response_str></flow></flow></presentation><resprocessing scoremodel="SumOfScores"><outcomes><decvar varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal" defaultval="0.0" minvalue="0.0" maxvalue="1.00"/></outcomes><respcondition title="correct"><conditionvar/><setvar variablename="SCORE" action="Set">SCORE.max</setvar><displayfeedback linkrefid="correct" feedbacktype="Response"/></respcondition><respcondition title="incorrect"><conditionvar><other/></conditionvar><setvar variablename="SCORE" action="Set">0.0</setvar><displayfeedback linkrefid="incorrect" feedbacktype="Response"/></respcondition></resprocessing><itemfeedback ident="correct" view="All"><flow_mat class="Block"><flow_mat class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="SMART_TEXT"/></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="incorrect" view="All"><flow_mat class="Block"><flow_mat class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="SMART_TEXT"/></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="solution" view="All"><solution view="All" feedbackstyle="Complete"><solutionmaterial><flow_mat class="Block"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="HTML">An elevator pitch is a short presentation, usually delivered in 30 seconds to one minute (about the time you spend in a large office elevator). You can use an elevator pitch to sell an idea to investors or clients, to introduce yourself, or to sell your candidacy to an employer.&lt;br&gt;A good elevator pitch is short, captures attention (with a story, statistics, or humour), is customized for a specific audience (choosing features and benefits for their needs), and is delivered confidently. A typical template could follow this pattern: the problem, your solution, benefits, why choose you over competitors, and a call to action. Use this pattern if you are given only a short time to pitch your product/idea to a potential investor. You can also develop an elevator pitch that introduces yourself. It would briefly tell who you who you are and what you do.</mat_formattedtext></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></solutionmaterial></solution></itemfeedback></item><item maxattempts="0"><itemmetadata><bbmd_asi_object_id>_188173_1</bbmd_asi_object_id><bbmd_asitype>Item</bbmd_asitype><bbmd_assessmenttype>Test</bbmd_assessmenttype><bbmd_sectiontype>Subsection</bbmd_sectiontype><bbmd_questiontype>Essay</bbmd_questiontype><bbmd_is_from_cartridge>false</bbmd_is_from_cartridge><bbmd_is_disabled>false</bbmd_is_disabled><bbmd_negative_points_ind>N</bbmd_negative_points_ind><bbmd_canvas_fullcrdt_ind>false</bbmd_canvas_fullcrdt_ind><bbmd_all_fullcredit_ind>false</bbmd_all_fullcredit_ind><bbmd_numbertype>none</bbmd_numbertype><bbmd_partialcredit/><bbmd_orientationtype>vertical</bbmd_orientationtype><bbmd_is_extracredit>false</bbmd_is_extracredit><bbmd_ai_state>No</bbmd_ai_state><qmd_absolutescore_max>1.000000000000000</qmd_absolutescore_max><qmd_weighting>0</qmd_weighting><qmd_instructornotes/></itemmetadata><presentation><flow class="Block"><flow class="QUESTION_BLOCK"><flow class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="HTML">Discuss how holograms could be used in business.</mat_formattedtext></mat_extension></material></flow></flow><flow class="RESPONSE_BLOCK"><response_str ident="response" rcardinality="Single" rtiming="No"><render_fib charset="us-ascii" encoding="UTF_8" rows="8" columns="127" maxchars="0" prompt="Box" fibtype="String" minnumber="0" maxnumber="0"/></response_str></flow></flow></presentation><resprocessing scoremodel="SumOfScores"><outcomes><decvar varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal" defaultval="0.0" minvalue="0.0" maxvalue="1.00"/></outcomes><respcondition title="correct"><conditionvar/><setvar variablename="SCORE" action="Set">SCORE.max</setvar><displayfeedback linkrefid="correct" feedbacktype="Response"/></respcondition><respcondition title="incorrect"><conditionvar><other/></conditionvar><setvar variablename="SCORE" action="Set">0.0</setvar><displayfeedback linkrefid="incorrect" feedbacktype="Response"/></respcondition></resprocessing><itemfeedback ident="correct" view="All"><flow_mat class="Block"><flow_mat class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="SMART_TEXT"/></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="incorrect" view="All"><flow_mat class="Block"><flow_mat class="FORMATTED_TEXT_BLOCK"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="SMART_TEXT"/></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="solution" view="All"><solution view="All" feedbackstyle="Complete"><solutionmaterial><flow_mat class="Block"><material><mat_extension><mat_formattedtext type="HTML">If you&amp;#x27;ve ever wanted to be in two places at once, your wish may soon come true. At a recent executive meeting of the global management and technology consulting firm Accenture, attendees included CEO Pierre Nanterme and human resources chief Ellyn Shook.&lt;br&gt;During the meeting, which took place near Chicago, they chatted with other managers, pitched and listened to ideas, and even shared a few ceremonial fist bumps. Nothing remarkable about that–except that Nanterme was in Paris and Shook was in New York City. Their three-dimensional selves were beamed in as holograms over the company&amp;#x27;s hyper-advanced information network.&lt;br&gt;Accenture has long been on the leading edge of communication technology, including the use of advanced telepresence facilities that help its huge workforce stay connected from outposts around the world. As much as Nanterme would like to meet frequently with employees in person, having 375,000 employees spread over 120 countries makes that impossible. In this context, holograms are created by scanning a person or object, vastly oversimplified. Scanning an object with a laser, transmitting the resulting data to a second location, then recreating the person or object as a three-dimensional &amp;quot;figure.&amp;quot; The figure is made entirely of light, but today&amp;#x27;s systems can make the figure look extremely lifelike. Researchers at the University of Tokyo have invented a system that combines holograms with ultrasonic haptic technology that simulates the sensation of touch, making it possible to &amp;quot;touch&amp;quot; a hologram.&lt;br&gt;Few companies have the resources to do what Accenture can with holograms, and as a technology consulting firm, it has other business reasons to keep pushing the limits of technology. If this use of holograms becomes mainstream, it could change the way geographically dispersed companies communicate. Holograms are already being used in areas such as research and product design, letting people interact with objects that are not physically present.</mat_formattedtext></mat_extension></material></flow_mat></solutionmaterial></solution></itemfeedback></item></section></assessment></questestinterop>